The task attached two kinds of DELIVERY evidence, as frontmatter citations. Each was
expanded to the exact lines it names; you are seeing the cited lines, not the whole
file. An observation cites the session transcript by ABSOLUTE path and each cited
line you see is a tool_result the session produced; an artifact cites a produced
file REPO-RELATIVE and each cited line is read from the tree.

OBSERVATIONS — proof the work happened, cited into the session transcript. These
should show a command running AND its result: a test run that came back green, a
build that succeeded, output that is itself the evidence.

